      "credit": "Own work",
      "source": "Sindh monument at chaukhandi pakistan",
      "description": "Sindh Monument at Chaukhandi, Pakistan.The Chaukhandi tombs form an early Islamic cemetery. Chakuandi, Sindh, Pakistan.The style of architecture is typical to the region of Sindh. Generally, the tombs are attributed to the Jokhio and known as the family graveyard of the Jokhio tribe, although other, mainly Baloch, tribes have also been buried here. They were mainly built during Mughal rule sometime in the 15th and 18th centuries when Islam became dominant.",
